# i18n (EN / AR)

Cureva is bilingual. Phase 2 Week 1 makes UI locale the foundation for every new screen.

## Product rules

- Locales: `en` | `ar`
- Direction: `ltr` | `rtl` on `document.documentElement`
- Persist via `setLocale` (cookie and/or localStorage)
- UI namespaces (Phase 2): `common`, `auth`, `practitioner`, `queue`, `notes`, `reports`, `settings`, `errors`
- No new Phase 2 user-facing string hard-coded English-only

## Entity bilingual fields (already shipping)

Catalog and people records use `name` + `nameAr` (later `bio` + `bioAr`).

- Prefer `BilingualNameFields` / the same EN+AR pattern
- Arabic inputs use `dir="rtl"` on the field
- Display prefers active locale, falls back to the other name when empty
- Persist both fields through DTO + `@clinic/types`

## UI copy (after i18n module lands)

Put the implemented module under `apps/web/src/` (likely `i18n/`) and update this rule if the path differs.

1. Add EN and AR keys in the same change
2. Wire UI through the project `t` / locale helper - no hardcoded Phase 2 labels
3. Prefer logical CSS (`ms-`, `me-`, `ps-`, `pe-`, `start`/`end`) for RTL
4. One i18n system only - match whatever Week 1 implements; do not add a second library beside it

## Do not

- Ship EN keys without AR
- Hardcode toast/button/nav copy on Phase 2 screens after i18n exists
- Add `safeT` / ad hoc dictionaries when `t` exists
